Z||000004||jelly2m8||09-10-2001||09:05 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by skitime:<BR><B>Congratulations.  Did you get a digital camera?  We recognized all the cars in that picture.  How is everyone doing?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR> Nope, I'm using a video camera, and I cant seem to be able to focus it worth a darn.<BR>Everytbody is doing ok Skitime, Lori has takin a new management job, I'm busy as heck.<BR> We still havent been able to get down your way yet, can't find a rental under $1000.00<BR> I think I'm just going to do a day rental, and unplug the speedometer.....hehe, the rental fees are good, but it is the price per kilometer which is the killer. 50 cents a kilometer really adds up when your thinkin 3200 kilometers!<P> I did get the fastback cleaned up alot, and have been trying to keep it that way, although the clutch MC has decided it has been on the car long enough.<P> I put new brakes all the way around on the V8, but I broke something in the right rear suspension the other week while doing some burnouts...;p havent had time to look at that yet. I think I found the problem with the stiff gas pedal . I checked it and there is 25" of vacuum in the engine. I also noticed that it stops pulling hard at 4k rpm. I have 5.0l heads on there, and apparently they arent flowing enough. I'm looking for 5.7L heads now. I'm also talking with a engine shop on making my flywheel heavier.<P> Loris fiero is still running great, at least one of the three is running 100%...hehe<P> <p>[This message has been edited by jelly2m8 (edited 09-10-2001).]||||reg||1
